# Per-Dockerfile ignore file (BuildKit feature: <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore
# in the build context, matched instead of the top-level .dockerignore when
# building with `-f archive_backfill/Dockerfile`). Keeps this job's build
# context scoped to just what it COPYs, without touching or being affected
# by the root .dockerignore that governs the live pipeline's own image.
#
# Same allowlist approach as the root .dockerignore: ignore everything by
# default, then explicitly un-ignore what archive_backfill/Dockerfile COPYs.
*

!archive_backfill
!archive_backfill/**
!source
!source/**
!models
!models/**

# Rules below apply AFTER the negations above (last-match-wins), so they
# re-exclude anything under archive_backfill/** that shouldn't ride along
# just because the directory as a whole is allowlisted -- most importantly
# a real .env (Cloud Run gets its secrets via --set-secrets/--set-env-vars,
# never a baked-in file), plus compiled bytecode and this job's own data/
# scratch output.
archive_backfill/.env
archive_backfill/.env.*
!archive_backfill/.env.local
archive_backfill/data
archive_backfill/logs
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
